Currently having the same issue, I've figured out a repro:

```javascript
const fastify = require('fastify')
const fs = require('fs')
const server = fastify()

server.get('/', (req, res) => {
  return res.send(fs.createReadStream('/dev/random'))
})

server.listen(3000)
``` 

Curl the stream
``` bash
$ curl -o /dev/null http://localhost:3000/
```
Hitting `Ctrl+C` to cancel the client request will crash the server:

```
_http_outgoing.js:489
    throw new Error('Can\'t set headers after they are sent.');
    ^

Error: Can't set headers after they are sent.
